-#define         MAX_CMD_GROUP   8
+/* HAND-PATCH to MCC-generated code, documented exception (docs/mcc-generated-code-patches.md).
+ * Raised from the MCC default of 8. The project registers eight command groups
+ * already - Test, env, lan, span, noip, testserver, bootload from the
+ * application, plus tcpip and iperf from the Harmony stack - and
+ * SYS_CMD_ADDGRP() has no way to report "table full" other than a return value
+ * nobody sees: the ninth registration simply does not happen. That is not a
+ * theoretical limit. Adding 'bootload' silently cost the 'span' group
+ * (mirror/sniffer) on 2026-09-04, because MIRROR_Initialize() is deferred to
+ * APP_STATE_SERVICE_TASKS and therefore registers last: the commands were gone
+ * from a running board with nothing in the log but one line,
+ * "MIRROR: SYS_CMD_ADDGRP failed". Costs ~16 bytes of RAM per unused slot. */
+#define         MAX_CMD_GROUP   12
 
 
